% \input{characteristics/description/HVAC Heating Efficiency}
The presence and efficiency of the primary heating system in the housing unit. This is the main input that determines the modeled heating system.

\paragraph{Distribution Data Sources}
% \input{characteristics/sources/HVAC Heating Efficiency}
\begin{itemize}
    \item The sample counts and sample weights are constructed using U.S.~EIA 2020 RECS microdata. 
    \item Shipment data based on ENERGY STAR ASHP shipments data and ENERGY STAR furnace shipments data. Efficiency data from Home Energy Saver are combined with age of equipment data from RECS. 
    \item Alaska-specific distribution is based on Alaska Retrofit Information System (2008 to 2022), maintained by Alaska Housing Finance Corporation.
\end{itemize}

\paragraph{Direct Conditional Dependencies}
\input{characteristics/dependencies/HVAC Heating Efficiency}

\paragraph{Options}
The options of the HVAC Heating Efficiency characteristic are shown in Table \ref{table:hc_opt_hvac_heating_efficiency} and assign the heating system type and efficiency. The system types are ducted ASHPs, electric baseboard, electric boiler, electric furnace, electric wall furnace, fuel boiler, fuel furnace, fuel wall/floor furnace, MSHPs, none, and shared heating. The Shared Heating option does not specify any properties. Shared Heating designates heating systems that serve multiple housing units in a multifamily building, and they have their own characteristics that set the properties; see Section \ref{sec:shared_systems}.

\input{characteristics/options/HVAC Heating Efficiency}

Property definitions are shown in Table (Table \ref{table:hc_arg_def_hvac_heating_efficiency}). See the OpenStudio-HPXML \href{https://openstudio-hpxml.readthedocs.io/en/v1.10.0/workflow_inputs.html#hpxml-heating-systems}{Heating System} documentation for additional information.

\input{characteristics/properties/HVAC Heating Efficiency}

\paragraph{Distribution Assumptions}
% \input{characteristics/assumptions/HVAC Heating Efficiency}
\begin{itemize}
